    {
      "title": "2.1.1 Evolution from Basic LLMs to LLM-Powered Agents.\nEarly LLMs excelled in in-context learning (ICL) but essentially op-\nerated as standalone text generators, lacking mechanisms for inter-\nacting with external environments or dynamically verifying gen-\nerated knowledge. A pivotal advancement was the emergence of\nstructured reasoning frameworks, such as Chain-of-Thought(CoT)\n[41]. This transformed the inference workload from a single query-\nresponse transaction into a longer, sequential reasoning process,\nimplicitly introducing early workflow semantics.",
